{
  "name": "Mathematics and Life: Conference celebrates International Day of Mathematics",
  "parent_id": 203313772661931,
  "group_id": "74773c50-859d-4dee-ab98-3809649cc502",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-31T09:29:26.805Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T14:59:54.678Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T14:59:54.660Z",
  "id": 203983121679976,
  "uuid": "3c6f91bf-0887-4516-890b-1c0309e94635",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "26d1a7af-7168-a2ef-3735-9ebc2295758d",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "9900ea6a-b2b9-4417-a4dc-1da411383fca",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "In his welcome note, Professor Farid Panjwani, Dean AKU-IED said: \"Mathematics is not isolated and confined to our schoolbooks. It is present in every aspect of our lives.\" He added that the purpose of this conference is to see how mathematics is connected to the various other disciplines we study in school and more importantly, the connection of mathematics with multiple aspects of our lives.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Talking about the place of Metacognition in the mathematics classroom, Dr Lee Ngan Hoe, from the ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "National Institute of Education, Singapore",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://www.nie.edu.sg/",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_self",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " stressed the need for a connection between online and offline classroom teaching with metacognitive practices. He discussed how without metacognition, connections between mathematics and various other disciplines cannot be made.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Professor José Antonio Martinez Aroza of ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "University of Granada, Spain",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://www.ugr.university/",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_self",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " discussed the beautiful connection between mathematics and architecture. He took the example of the Alhambra Palace and Fortress Complex to show how aesthetically pleasing results are achieved through various mathematical structures found in this architectural wonder.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Following a similar theme, Professor Fozia S. Kazi of the ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Islamic University of Science & Technology, India",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://www.iust.ac.in/",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_self",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", surveyed the use of mathematical tools of symmetry analysis to answer questions about cultural agency in Kashmir. She discussed how patterns found on Kashmiri decorated forms including the geometric patterns found on tiles, shawls, lattices, khatamband, carpets and metalwork can be connected to mathematics.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Professor Jayasree Subramanian at the ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "SRM University, Andhra Pradesh",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://srmap.edu.in/",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_self",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", India highlighted the connection between mathematics, language and the socio-economic background of learners. She challenged the idea that the language of mathematics is universal because while teaching in a classroom, one has to often explain concepts in the local language for the sake of better understanding and local language only develops within a socio-economic context.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Professor Bal Chandra Luitel of ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Kathmandu University, Nepal",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://ku.edu.np/",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_self",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", stressed the need of shifting from conventional mathematics teaching to a programme that deals with the subject while keeping the global socio-political context in mind. Similarly, Professor Munirah Ghazali of the ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "University of Malaysia",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://www.um.edu.my/",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_self",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " discussed the need for changing the way mathematics is taught to incorporate skill-based learning to contribute to achieve Sustainable Development Goals.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The talks held during these two days will eventually lead to a publication titled 'Mathematics Unites: Insights from South and Southeast Contexts'. The publication will attempt to challenge the narrow vision of the subject which is often prevalent among students and teachers and unite mathematical ideas with culture and human societies.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
